Linux check in Docker (native arm64 on Apple silicon). Needs a running Docker.
Run: scripts/linux-check/run.sh [SOURCE_DIR] [build test clippy snap release]   (default: this checkout, build test clippy snap).
It mounts the source read-only and copies it in; cargo's cache and target live in docker volumes kot-linux-cargo and kot-linux-target.
Logs and snaps go to /tmp/linux-check/<folder name>/. `release` also builds the release binaries and reports the stripped size.
Remove the volumes with: docker volume rm kot-linux-cargo kot-linux-target
Headless snaps need a software GL renderer that supports f16 shaders: Debian trixie's Mesa does (WGPU_BACKEND=gl, the default here).
Adapted from Uzumaki's scripts/linux-check.
